{"n":"Dia","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":36.725058,"lo":-4.415113,"d":915,"h":"Mo-Sa 09:00-21:30; Jun-Sep Su 09:00-15:00; PH \"abre algunos festivos\""},{"n":"Banco Sabadell","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":36.722788,"lo":-4.420374,"d":919},{"n":"Santander Bank","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":36.72188,"lo":-4.421524,"d":933},{"n":"Plaza de toros de La Malagueta","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.720333,"lo":-4.410806,"d":419,"ds":"La Malagueta is a bullring at Málaga, Andalucía, Spain. It is located in the eastern district of Málaga, in its namesake neighbourhood of La Malagueta. The first event was held in 1876.","wpu":"Plaza de toros de La Malagueta","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/M%C3%A1laga_La_Malagueta_01.jpg/960px-M%C3%A1laga_La_Malagueta_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Alcazaba of Málaga","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.721389,"lo":-4.415556,"d":538,"ds":"The Alcazaba is a palatial fortification in Málaga, Spain, built during the period of Muslim-ruled Al-Andalus. The current complex was begun in the 11th century and was modified or rebuilt multiple times up to the 14th century. It is one of the best-preserved alcazabas in Spain.","wpu":"Alcazaba of Málaga","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Alcazaba_de_M%C3%A1laga_overview.jpg/960px-Alcazaba_de_M%C3%A1laga_overview.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Palacio de Buenavista","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.721667,"lo":-4.418333,"d":703,"ds":"Buenavista Palace (Spanish: El Palacio de Buenavista or El Palacio de los Condes de Buenavista, \"the palace of the counts of Buenavista\") is a historical edifice in Málaga, Andalusia, Spain. It was built in the first half of the 16th century for Diego de Cazalla on the ruins of a Nasrid palace.","wpu":"Palacio de Buenavista","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/MPM_2.jpg/960px-MPM_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"English Cemetery, Málaga","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.7212,"lo":-4.4071,"d":703,"ds":"The English Cemetery in Málaga (Spanish: Cementerio Inglés de Málaga), or Anglican Cemetery, or Cemetery of St George, is the oldest non-Roman Catholic Christian cemetery established on mainland Spain.","wpu":"English Cemetery, Málaga","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cementerio_Ingl%C3%A9s.jpg/960px-Cementerio_Ingl%C3%A9s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Málaga Cathedral","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.720042,"lo":-4.42012,"d":719,"ds":"The Cathedral of Málaga is a Roman Catholic church in the city of Málaga in Andalusia in southern Spain. It is in the Renaissance architectural tradition. The cathedral is located within the limits defined by a now missing portion of the medieval Moorish walls, the remains of which surround the nearby Alcazaba and the Castle of Gibralfaro.","wpu":"Málaga Cathedral","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/Torrecatedralypalmeras.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Plaza de la Merced","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.7234,"lo":-4.4175,"d":816,"ds":"Plaza de la Merced is a public square located in the barrio La Merced in central Málaga, Spain. The plaza has been a part of the city since the city of Málaga's Roman era, and has been operating as a town market place since at least the fifteenth century. It is one of the largest public squares in Málaga’s city center, and is also known for containing Pablo Picasso's childhood home.","wpu":"Plaza de la Merced","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Malaga%2C_on_the_square_%22Plaza_de_la_Merced%22%2C_image_1.JPG/960px-Malaga%2C_on_the_square_%22Plaza_de_la_Merced%22%2C_image_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Reding Fountain","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.721503,"lo":-4.405339,"d":846,"ds":"The Reding Fountain is a historic 17th-century fountain located in the Andalusian city of Málaga, Spain. It has been reproduced countless times by local painters. It is located at one end of the Príes Avenue and pipes spring water from the Mount Gibralfaro.","wpu":"Reding Fountain","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Reding_Fountain.jpg/960px-Reding_Fountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Carmen Thyssen Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.721389,"lo":-4.422778,"d":998,"ds":"The Carmen Thyssen Museum (Museo Carmen Thyssen Málaga) is an art museum in the Spanish city Málaga. The main focus of the museum is 19th-century Spanish painting, predominantly Andalusian, based on the collection of Carmen Cervera, fifth wife of Baron Hans Heinrich Thyssen-Bornemisza. Since 1992 the Thyssen family's art collection has been on display at the Thyssen-Bornemisza Museum in Madrid.","wpu":"Carmen Thyssen Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Palacio_de_Villal%C3%B3n.jpg/960px-Palacio_de_Villal%C3%B3n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Museum Jorge Rando","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.7268,"lo":-4.4238,"d":1453,"ds":"The Museum Jorge Rando is the first expressionist museum in Málaga, Andalusia, Spain. Dedicated to the painter Jorge Rando, it collects his works and it temporally hosts the works of other national and international artists belonging to this movement. It was officially inaugurated on May 28, 2015.","wpu":"Museum Jorge Rando","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Museumjorgerando.JPG/960px-Museumjorgerando.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Al-Andalus Mosque","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.7192,"lo":-4.4383,"d":2268,"ds":"Al-Andalus Mosque (Spanish: Mezquita de al-Ándalus) is a Sunni Islam mosque in the neighbourhood of Arroyo del Cuarto city of Málaga, Andalusia, Spain.","wpu":"Al-Andalus Mosque","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Mezquita_de_al-%C3%81ndalus1.jpg/960px-Mezquita_de_al-%C3%81ndalus1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Málaga Public Library","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.7025,"lo":-4.444722,"d":3255,"ds":"The Málaga Public Library is a public library located in Málaga, Spain.","wpu":"Málaga Public Library","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Biblioteca_de_M%C3%A1laga.jpg/960px-Biblioteca_de_M%C3%A1laga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Jardín Botánico La Concepción","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.762222,"lo":-4.426667,"d":5173,"ds":"The Jardín Botánico Histórico La Concepción is a landscape garden with over one hundred and fifty years of history. It is located at the northern entrance of the Spanish city of Málaga. This garden is one of the few gardens with subtropical plants that exist in Europe.","wpu":"Jardín Botánico La Concepción","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Botanic_Garden_La_Concepcion_Malaga_edited_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Botanic_Garden_La_Concepcion_Malaga_edited_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"wk":"2026-10-18","about":{"ds":"Málaga ( ; Spanish: [ˈmalaɣa] ) is a municipality of Spain and the capital of the province of Málaga, in the autonomous community of Andalusia. With a population of 597,173 in 2025, it is the 2nd-largest city in Andalusia and the 6th-largest in the country. It lies in Southern Iberia on the Costa del Sol ('Coast of the Sun') of the Mediterranean, primarily on the left bank of the Guadalhorce.","wpu":"Málaga","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Da_Gibralfaro_%28cropped%292.jpg/960px-Da_Gibralfaro_%28cropped%292.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}}